Frost occurs when the temperature is at or below 0°C (32°F) and moisture in the air condenses and freezes.
Frost does not necessarily indicate that it will snow.
Snow occurs when there is precipitation, which is not always present when frost forms.
#### No. (Score: 0.22026023268699646)

